  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "\"Good morning, class!\" says Teacher Kim. \"This is May.\" She is new. \"Hi, class!\" says May. \"Hello, May!\" say the children. May smiles. \"What is your name?\" asks a boy. \"My name is May,\" says the girl. \"How do you spell May?\" asks Leo. \"M-A-Y,\" says May.",
      "\"How old are you?\" asks Lily. \"I am seven,\" says May. \"Where do you live?\" asks Teacher Kim. \"I live next to the school,\" says May. \"It is a white house.\" \"Have you got a brother or a sister?\" asks Lily. \"I have got a brother,\" says May. \"His name is Pat.\" \"Is he a baby?\" asks Leo. \"No, he is not!\" says May. \"He is five.\"",
      "\"What is your favorite lesson?\" asks Teacher Kim. \"English!\" says May. \"Good!\" says Teacher Kim. \"Thank you, May,\" says Teacher Kim. Now the class has ten girls and nine boys. May is Lily's new classmate. She sits next to Lily. Lily smiles. At three o'clock, Lily says, \"Goodbye, May!\" \"Goodbye, Lily!\" says May. May is happy at her new school."
    ],
